# Room-key epochs and rotation. Each room has a symmetric AES-256 key per epoch;
# payloads name their key_epoch. Join and leave both rotate. Keys are HPKE-wrapped
# to each member's DEVICE keys (the member root holds no live secret).
direction: right

e1: "Epoch 1\n(room created)" {
  style.fill: "#eff6ff"
  k: "room_key₁" { shape: circle; style.fill: "#dbeafe" }
  m: "wrapped → Alice's devices" { style.font-size: 12 }
}
e2: "Epoch 2\n(Bob added)" {
  style.fill: "#ecfdf5"
  k: "room_key₂" { shape: circle; style.fill: "#bbf7d0" }
  m: "wrapped → Alice + Bob devices" { style.font-size: 12 }
}
e3: "Epoch 3\n(Bob removed)" {
  style.fill: "#fef2f2"
  k: "room_key₃" { shape: circle; style.fill: "#fecaca" }
  m: "wrapped → Alice's devices ONLY" { style.font-size: 12 }
}

e1 -> e2: "MEMBER_ADD\n{ epoch:2, wrapped_keys }" { style.stroke: "#047857" }
e2 -> e3: "MEMBER_REMOVE + ROOM_KEY_ROTATE\n{ epoch:3, wrapped_keys }" { style.stroke: "#b91c1c" }

note: |md
  **Pre-join history is opaque** — a new member gets only current+future epoch
  keys (same property as Megolm). **Post-removal is opaque** to the removed member,
  but messages they already held stay readable: rotation protects the *future*, not
  the past. Wrapping is DHKEM(X25519,HKDF-SHA256)/AES-256-GCM over each device's
  Ed25519 key mapped to X25519.
| { style.font-size: 13; near: bottom-center }
